# Acknowledgements

## Dr Anna Parimalam

This website, containing all of Anna's works and maintained by the Arignar Anna Trust, was started so that admirers of Anna, students, and the general public throughout the world may study them free of charge.

Anna's beloved son, Dr Anna Parimalam, worked with great dedication until the end of his life to bring all of Anna's works into print. Accordingly, almost all the works have appeared through several publishers. During his final years, I worked with him in Anna-related service for nearly five years. After his unexpected death, we have continued the work he left behind. His final wish was that all of Anna's works should appear online as a digital library. With that aim, this website was planned and has now been published on behalf of the Arignar Anna Trust (Registered No. 1135/2011, Thanjavur), which we founded. My experience of working with Dr Anna Parimalam has been of immense help. We will never forget him and are striving to complete the tasks he left behind.

Anna's works published so far comprise about 26,000 pages. In the first phase, we intend to add these pages as quickly as possible. In the next phase, we plan to search for any further works by Anna that may still be available.

We are very happy to maintain this website as one of the activities of the Arignar Anna Trust. Through the Trust, we also carry out public service in Anna's way. We request admirers of Anna to support our work to the extent they can.

Contributions may be made through the website or by cheque or demand draft in the name of ARIGNAR ANNA TRUST.

